{"step_index":320,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:22:38Z","content":"All changes are complete. Here's a summary of everything implemented:\n\n---\n\n### Smart Fallback (No More `alert()`)\n- The crude `alert('No conjunction selected...')` is completely gone. When **⚠ JUMP TO TCA** is clicked with nothing selected, the system automatically searches `window._cachedConjunctions` (populated when the Live Tracking table loads) and picks the **highest-risk CRITICAL event** (e.g., COSMOS 2251 DEB vs STARLINK-1007). It then auto-sets all the required state (TCA time, conjunction pair) and proceeds seamlessly.\n\n### Precision Clock Jump\n- The Cesium clock is snapped to the exact TCA `JulianDate`, the animation is paused, and both the slider position and time label are updated to reflect the precise encounter moment.\n\n### Dual-Object Dynamic Framing\n- Instead of locking onto a single satellite, the camera calculates the **3D midpoint** between both conjunction objects using `Cesium.Cartesian3.midpoint()`. It then executes a cinematic `viewer.camera.flyTo()` to a vantage point 200 km offset on three axes, looking down at the encounter zone with the 4K Earth visible beneath.\n\n### Encounter Telemetry Overlay\n- A glassmorphism card titled **// CONJUNCTION ENCOUNTER (TCA)** with a pulsing red radar dot slides into view at the top-left of the 3D viewer, displaying:\n  - **Primary** / **Secondary** object names\n  - **Miss Distance at TCA** (e.g., 1.20 km)\n  - **Collision Probability (Pc)** (e.g., 1.42e-4)\n  - **Relative Velocity** (e.g., 14.2 km/s)\n- A glowing red proximity laser (`PolylineGlowMaterialProperty`) is drawn between the two objects using a `CallbackProperty` so it updates every frame.\n- The **[ Resume Simulation ▶ 10x ]** button unpauses the clock at 10x speed, highlights the matching speed button, and hides the overlay so you can watch the objects fly past each other.\n\n**Please refresh your browser at http://localhost:3000**. Switch directly to the 3D Orbit Viewer tab (without clicking any table row), and click **⚠ JUMP TO TCA**. The system will auto-select the critical conjunction and cinematically frame the encounter!"}
{"step_index":321,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T20:28:21Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\"Navigating the 3D globe with a mouse or trackpad is feeling clunky. Let's add a virtual on-screen joystick (like a drone controller) to smoothly fly the camera around the Earth.\n\nPlease update index.html and app.js with the following implementation:\n\n1. Import the Joystick Library (index.html)\n\nIn the <head>, import the Nipple.js library:\n<script src=\"[https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/nipplejs/0.10.1/nipplejs.min.js](https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/nipplejs/0.10.1/nipplejs.min.js)\"></script>\n\nInside the '3D ORBIT VIEWER' container, add a dedicated div for the joystick. Position it in the bottom-left corner using Tailwind (e.g., absolute bottom-10 left-10 w-32 h-32 z-50). Give it an ID like joystick-zone.\n\n2. Initialize the Joystick (app.js)\n\nCreate a global object to store the joystick's current movement data: let joystickInput = { x: 0, y: 0, active: false };\n\nInitialize the joystick inside the joystick-zone element:\n\nJavaScript\nconst joystickManager = nipplejs.create({\n    zone: document.getElementById('joystick-zone'),\n    mode: 'static',\n    position: { left: '50%', top: '50%' },\n    color: '#06b6d4', // Cyan to match our HUD\n    size: 100\n});\nAdd event listeners to update the data when the user drags the stick:\n\nOn joystickManager.on('move', (evt, data)): Set joystickInput.active = true; joystickInput.x = data.vector.x; joystickInput.y = data.vector.y;\n\nOn joystickManager.on('end'): Reset joystickInput.active = false; joystickInput.x = 0; joystickInput.y = 0;\n\n3. Bind to the Camera Engine (app.js)\n\nTo make the movement butter-smooth, we hook into Cesium's render loop. Inside your existing viewer.clock.onTick event listener, add this logic:\n\nJavaScript\nif (joystickInput.active && !viewer.trackedEntity) {\n    const speed = 0.02; // Adjust for camera sensitivity\n    // Note: Nipple.js Y-axis is inverted relative to Cesium's rotateUp\n    viewer.scene.camera.rotateRight(joystickInput.x * speed);\n    viewer.scene.camera.rotateUp(joystickInput.y * speed);\n}\nAction: Write the updated code. Once the server reloads, open the 3D Viewer. Use the new cyan thumbstick in the bottom left to smoothly pan the camera around the Earth, and take a screenshot showing the joystick UI in action.\"\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-24T01:58:21+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
